  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"Approved recordings already exist for each voice part, and a shared folder can pair them with bar numbers and brief rehearsal notes.\", \"decision\": \"How should practice recordings be made easy to use?\", \"goal\": \"Make rehearsals easy to attend and prepare for while helping singers use shared rehearsal time effectively.\", \"problem\": \"A community choir is preparing a small program through a series of rehearsals. It has a conductor, willing section leaders, a booking organizer, numbered scores that members may use, and shared practice recordings. The rehearsal room has movable chairs and enough space for short sectional work. Members have varied experience and availability. Musical direction remains with the conductor, and each routine below can operate within any agreed rehearsal schedule.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nSection leaders send their singers a short ordered list of approved recordings with bar numbers after each rehearsal. The practice sequence reflects that section’s immediate needs without requiring members to search the entire recording folder.\nThe conductor groups approved recordings by difficult passage and lists each available voice part within that passage. Singers begin with the shared rehearsal problem and select their own line from the materials associated with it.\nThe organizer groups approved recordings by voice part and adds the bar numbers highlighted during rehearsal. Singers can locate their own material first and then move directly to the passages most relevant to current practice."
    }
  ],
